.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt ZONEFILE-GO 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm zonefile-go
.Nd generate Unbound and NSD zone data
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl o Ar path
.Op Fl s Ar serialfile
.Op Fl t Cm unbound | nsd
.Nm
.Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads forward zones, hosts and reverse networks from a configuration file
in the format described in
.Xr zonefile.conf 5
and writes the zone data for
.Xr unbound 8
or
.Xr nsd 8 .
PTR records are generated from the addresses of the hosts, for the
networks declared as reverse zones.
.Pp
The configuration is checked completely before anything is written.
All errors are reported, one per line, in the form
.Ar file : Ns Ar line : message .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar file
Read the configuration from
.Ar file .
If
.Ar file
is
.Sq - ,
read it from standard input; relative include paths are then resolved
against the current directory.
The default is
.Pa /etc/zonefile.conf .
.It Fl n
Configtest mode.
Only check the configuration file for validity and print
.Dq configuration OK
to standard error.
Nothing is written and the serial is not changed.
.It Fl o Ar path
Where to write the output.
For
.Cm unbound ,
.Ar path
is a file, written atomically; without
.Fl o
the output goes to standard output.
For
.Cm nsd ,
.Ar path
is a directory, by default
.Pa nsd .
.It Fl s Ar serialfile
Keep the last serial in
.Ar serialfile .
The default is
.Pa .serial
in the current directory.
.It Fl t Cm unbound | nsd
The output format.
The default is
.Cm unbound .
.Bl -tag -width unbound
.It Cm unbound
A fragment of
.Xr unbound.conf 5
with a
.Ic server
clause and one
.Ic local-zone
with its
.Ic local-data
and
.Ic local-data-ptr
statements per zone.
.It Cm nsd
The file
.Pa zones.conf ,
with one
.Ic zone
clause per zone for inclusion into
.Xr nsd.conf 5 ,
and one zone file per zone in the subdirectory
.Pa master .
Every file is written atomically, the zone files before
.Pa zones.conf .
Zone files named in the previous
.Pa zones.conf
whose zones are no longer configured are removed afterwards and reported
on standard error.
Other files in
.Pa master
are left alone.
.El
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Ss Serial numbers
Unless a zone sets a fixed serial with
.Ic serial ,
all zones get the same serial in the format
.Ar YYYYMMDDnn :
the current date in UTC with
.Ar nn
set to 00, or the previous serial plus one if that is larger.
Several runs on one day therefore count up, and the serial never goes
back.
The new serial is stored in the serial file only after the output has been
written.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/zonefile.conf" -compact
.It Pa /etc/zonefile.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Pa .serial
Default serial file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check a configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zonefile-go -n -f /etc/zonefile.conf
.Ed
.Pp
Generate local data for
.Xr unbound 8
and reload it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zonefile-go -s /var/unbound/etc/zonefile.serial \e
	-o /var/unbound/etc/zones.conf
# unbound-control reload
.Ed
.Pp
with
.Bd -literal -offset indent
include: "/var/unbound/etc/zones.conf"
.Ed
.Pp
in
.Pa /var/unbound/etc/unbound.conf .
.Pp
Generate zones for
.Xr nsd 8
and reload them:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zonefile-go -t nsd -o /var/nsd/zones -s /var/nsd/zonefile.serial
# nsd-control reconfig && nsd-control reload
.Ed
.Pp
with
.Bd -literal -offset indent
include: "/var/nsd/zones/zones.conf"
.Ed
.Pp
in
.Pa /var/nsd/etc/nsd.conf .
The
.Ic zonefile
paths in
.Pa zones.conf
start with
.Pa master/ ,
so
.Ic zonesdir
in
.Xr nsd.conf 5
has to be the output directory,
.Pa /var/nsd/zones
here.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nsd.conf 5 ,
.Xr unbound.conf 5 ,
.Xr zonefile.conf 5 ,
.Xr nsd 8 ,
.Xr unbound 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
succeeds zonefile, written in Python, and zonefile-rs, written in Rust,
which read YAML or TOML.
For the same zones it writes the same records.
